    "body": "A linear coefficient checksum can have a known target for every legal one-per-color tuple by assigning one weight per color. This change checks the limitation of that filter: the common-target condition forces within-color equality, and natural partial vectors then have at most(K+1)^m distinct checksum values when each color total is at most K. The hand independent-residue analysis uses that value image rather than the full overlapping representation count. [pcc:unverified]\n\nFour reusable laws in `Group.ColorChecksums` use existing finite-sum deletion/cancellation, natural scalar distribution and finite image/function-cardinality laws. The six-field prospective plan and inherited floor precede source. Actual prime-field point and ZMod endpoints apply the laws unchanged. Canonical gate001 audits219 theorems/0 failures/0 trusted-native exceptions; all4 named axiom prints use standard allowed axioms. No fresh checker or hosted pass is asserted. [pcc:unverified]\n\nFull report, DOT/SVG and inspected two-page PDF separate the formal image bound from its hand probability/asymptotic application. The universal target concerns all legal coefficient tuples, not just actual group-zero solutions. Adaptive/deterministic/nonlinear/group-dependent/joint filters remain outside the stated test. A joint coordinate-sensitive extractor and complete end-to-end construction/yield/recovery bound remain missing. [pcc:unverified]\n\nPCC-20261116-06676d is unverified with nine attestation subjects. The six-row owner ledger is an exact prefix and all41 older subject hashes remain intact. Failed source/logs and raw diagnostic spaces are retained; source/prose whitespace check exits0, full archival check exits2 on raw logs. No limit/trust/inventory/linter exception, numerical/native/qualification or paid execution. PR21 landing/hosted-failure receipts and its queued autonomy/outcome accompany this substantive assessment. Consumer frozen histories and monitors remain separate. [pcc:unverified]\n",
